does not account for an additional 4-byte header required for the deprecated binary subtype.

This oversight leads to a potential out-of-bounds read/write when processing BSON_TYPE_BINARY payloads with subtype `BSON_SUBTYPE_BINARY_DEPRECATED`. If the payload length exceeds the allocated buffer, memory corruption or other undefined behaviors can occur, which is a significant security risk.

