The vulnerability stems from insufficient validation of `ctx->mb_height` in conjunction with the `frame->interlaced_frame` and `ctx->height`. Specifically, the invalid condition combining `ctx->mb_height` and interlaced scenarios was overlooked, allowing potential logic errors and unsafe memory reads/writes.

The fix separates the two checks into independent conditions, ensuring proper validation of both cases.

### Program Slice (Code Related to the Vulnerability):
```c
