### Program Slicing: Parts of Code Contributing to the Security Vulnerability

The vulnerability exists because the code doesn't validate the stream's remaining length before reading additional data when bitmap compression headers are present. The security patch addresses this issue by adding a boundary check (`Stream_GetRemainingLength(s) < 8`) before reading the compressed bitmap data. Below is the sliced code relevant to this vulnerability:

```c
	if (bitmapData->flags & BITMAP_COMPRESSION)
