### Analyzed Vulnerability
The vulnerability lies in the lack of a check for `rs->rs_transport` being `NULL` before dereferencing it. If `rs->rs_transport` is `NULL`, this will cause a null pointer dereference and could lead to a kernel crash.

### Sliced Code
```c
	if (rs->rs_bound_addr == 0) {
		ret = -ENOTCONN; /* XXX not a great errno */
		goto out;
	}

	if (!rs->rs_transport->get_mr) {
		ret = -EOPNOTSUPP;
		goto out;
	}
```

### Relevant Snippet Based on Security Patch
Post the patch, the first condition is updated to check both `rs->rs_bound_addr` and `rs->rs_transport`, making sure neither is invalid before proceeding.

```c
	if (rs->rs_bound_addr == 0 || !rs->rs_transport) {
		ret = -ENOTCONN; /* XXX not a great errno */
		goto out;
	}
```

