### Explanation of Vulnerability

The vulnerability lies in the processing of filenames (`name_len`). Specifically:
1. The original code does not properly validate and filter out filenames that are blank or one-character long (e.g., "/"), leaving room for unintended behavior or misinterpretation of the files.
2. Such filenames might be incorrectly handled in subsequent operations, leading to undefined or insecure behavior. 

### Security Fix

The patch adds the following condition to ignore blank or one-character filenames:
```c
if (name_len < 2 || !name[0] || !name[1]) continue;
```
This ensures that filenames of length less than 2 or with invalid characters are skipped safely.

