The issue lies in the unsafe memory allocation using `xmalloc`. The calculation for the size in `xmalloc` can result in integer overflows if `lena`, `lenb`, or their combination exceeds the maximum representable size (`SIZE_MAX`). This can lead to improper memory allocation, potential buffer overflows, and security vulnerabilities.

### Program Slice:
The relevant portions of the code for the vulnerability are as follows:

```c
      if (ignore || translate)
