### Vulnerability Analysis
The vulnerability lies in the improper casting of `msg.sct.length` to `uint64_t` before passing it to `malloc`. This could potentially result in a buffer overflow due to unintended integer promotion or incorrect sizing calculations. By directly using `msg.sct.length`, which is already of the correct type, the patched version avoids such issues.

---

