### Program Slicing for Vulnerability Analysis

**Identified Vulnerability**:   
The original code has an "out of range" issue when comparing `partNumber` to the size of the `parts` vector. The condition `if (partNumber < 0 || partNumber > static_cast<int>(parts.size()))` is incorrect because `partNumber` valid values range from `0` to `parts.size() - 1`. The comparison `partNumber > static_cast<int>(parts.size())` should be `partNumber >= static_cast<int>(parts.size())`.

**Relevant Code Slice**:   
The vulnerability arises in the logic handling the validation of `partNumber`. Below is the sliced code highlighting the issue:

```cpp
// Extracted Vulnerable Code
if (partNumber < 0 || partNumber > static_cast<int>(parts.size()))
{
    throw IEX_NAMESPACE::IoExc("part number out of range");
}
```

**Security Patch**:   
The patch correctly changes the comparison operator from `>` to `>=` for the upper bound check:

```cpp
// Patched Code
if (partNumber < 0 || partNumber >= static_cast<int>(parts.size()))
{
    throw IEX_NAMESPACE::IoExc("part number out of range");
}
```

