#### Security Issue:
The vulnerability lies in the inappropriate use of the `uint16_t` type for the variable `keylen`. This may lead to improper handling of key lengths that exceed the range of an unsigned 16-bit integer, potentially causing buffer overflows or memory corruption when `keylen` is utilized for array indexing or memory operations.

#### Sliced Code:
The parts of the code relevant to the vulnerability and its fix are isolated below. These sections involve the declaration and calculation of `keylen`.

```c
